# Island: a 100 kohm pull-down on a processor pin that drives a modem input (DTR). From a real 12 V
# automotive board: R7 (100k +/-1 %, row C25741) and the nets from the export of `netsmith build`.
# ASSUMPTIONS: the pin's output resistances and leakage (as in gate_pulldown.cir).
# report: v(DTR) i(r7) p(r7)
# today: `current of part r7 is not known` (2 relations not evaluated, 1 note); the board states `dtr_hold_current == logic_supply.voltage / dtr_pulldown.resistance` by hand
V  rail  V3V3 GND 3.234..3.333
L  pin   DTR V3V3 GND states=HLZ roh=0..200 rol=0..200 rz=3.3M
R  r7    DTR GND 100k+-1%
